---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Loft Conversion St Neots | Truleum Cambridgeshire Specialists"
  description="Expert loft conversion services in St Neots, Cambridgeshire. Local team for dormer, Velux and bespoke loft builds across St Neots and surrounding villages."
>

  <main class="main-content area-stneots-page" style="font-family: 'Poppins', Arial, sans-serif;">

    <style>
      .area-stneots-page {
        --area-blue: #0a1a4a;
        --area-blue-2: #162b70;
        --area-gold: #d4af37;
        --area-soft: #f5f7fb;
        --area-text: #334155;
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }
      .area-wrap { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; }
      .area-stneots-page section,
      .area-stneots-page h1,
      .area-stneots-page h2,
      .area-stneots-page h3,
      .area-stneots-page p,
      .area-stneots-page img,
      .area-stneots-page a { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; }
      .area-hero { padding: 112px 0 96px; color: #fff; background: radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%, rgba(212,175,55,0.24) 0%, rgba(212,175,55,0) 45%), linear-gradient(132deg, #08163d 0%, #0a1a4a 45%, #1c347f 100%); }
      .area-hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.08fr 0.92fr; gap: 40px; align-items: center; }
      .area-kicker { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,232,159,0.98); color: #0a1a4a; border-radius: 999px; padding: 10px 18px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.6px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; }
      .area-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 58px); line-height: 1.1; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 15ch; }
      .area-hero p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92); margin: 0 0 26px; max-width: 60ch; }
      .area-hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 28px; }
      .area-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; padding: 14px 24px; }
      .area-btn-primary { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffe89f 0%, #9f7628 100%); color: #111827; }
      .area-btn-ghost { color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }
      .lc-metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 8px; }
      .lc-metric { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px; text-align: center; }
      .lc-metric strong { display: block; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1; color: #ffe89f; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .lc-metric span { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.84); }
      .area-hero-card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.11); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 20px; padding: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(8px); }
      .area-hero-card img { width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; }
      .area-price { margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; color: #0a1a4a; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
      .area-price strong { color: #111827; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-section { padding: 86px 0; }
      .area-head { text-align: center; max-width: 830px; margin: 0 auto 34px; }
      .area-head h2 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 12px; }
      .area-head p { color: #475569; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }
      .area-intro { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 26px; }
      .area-panel { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e4e9f2; border-radius: 16px; padding: 24px; box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05); }
      .area-panel h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
      .area-panel p { color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 14px; }
      .area-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 9px; }
      .area-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 9px; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-list i { color: var(--area-gold); margin-top: 3px; }
      .area-types-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 18px; }
      .area-type { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; padding: 20px; }
      .area-type h3 { font-size: 21px; color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-type p { margin: 0; color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-zone { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #102559 100%); }
      .area-zone .area-head h2, .area-zone .area-head p { color: #fff; }
      .area-zone-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
      .area-zone-item { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 { color: #ffe89f; font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a { color: #ffe89f; text-decoration: none; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .area-zone-item p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
      .area-proof-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
      .area-proof { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; text-align: center; padding: 20px; }
      .area-proof i { color: var(--area-gold); font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .area-proof h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 7px; }
      .area-proof p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
      .area-faq { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-faq-grid { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
      .area-faq-item { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; }
      .area-faq-item h3 { color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-faq-item p { margin: 0; color: #334155; line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-cta { padding: 88px 0; text-align: center; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #1f3a8a 100%); }
      .area-cta h2 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); }
      .area-cta p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 24px; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px; }
      @media (max-width: 1080px) { .area-types-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-zone-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      @media (max-width: 900px) { .area-hero { padding: 86px 0 70px; } .area-hero-grid, .area-columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-hero h1 { max-width: 100%; } }
      @media (max-width: 680px) { .lc-metrics { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-section, .area-cta { padding: 64px 0; } .area-types-grid, .area-zone-grid, .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-head p, .area-hero p, .area-cta p { font-size: 16px; } }
    </style>

    <section class="area-hero">
      <div class="area-wrap area-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="area-kicker"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> St Neots, Cambridgeshire</span>
          <h1>Loft Conversion St Neots For Growing Cambridgeshire Homes</h1>
          <p>Need a loft conversion in St Neots? As Cambridgeshire's fastest growing town, St Neots has a wide range of housing from Victorian terraces in the old town to newer detached and semi detached properties on modern developments. We plan every build around your specific roof and situation. See our <a href="/services/loft-conversion-cambridge-service/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">full Loft Conversion Service page</a> for more detail.</p>
          <div class="area-hero-actions">
            <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Get Free Survey <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a>
            <a href="/gallery/" class="area-btn area-btn-ghost">View Our Work</a>
          </div>
          <div class="lc-metrics">
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i></strong><span>Free Site Survey</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i></strong><span>Fully Insured</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-award"></i></strong><span>Quality Assured</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="area-hero-card">
          <img src="/wp-content/uploads/Loft-Conversion/loft-services-london.webp" alt="Loft conversion in St Neots Cambridgeshire by Truleum">
          <div class="area-price">
            <span>Typical project budget</span>
            <strong>From £28,000</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-intro">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Local Approach For Every Loft Conversion In St Neots</h2>
          <p>We plan each St Neots loft conversion around your roof structure, budget and how you want the room to work long term. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">homeowner guide</a> explains every stage from first survey to handover.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-columns">
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <p>Your St Neots loft conversion includes structural work, insulation, roof windows or dormers, first and second fix electrics and a quality finish throughout.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Written scope with clear stage pricing</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Regular project updates throughout the build</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Layout options for bedrooms, ensuites or home offices</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Full building regulations support from start to sign off</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>Why St Neots Homes Need Specialist Input</h3>
            <p>St Neots has grown rapidly and includes everything from original Victorian terraces to 2000s and 2010s new builds. Each generation of housing needs a different loft conversion approach. See the <a href="https://www.planningportal.co.uk/permission/common-projects/loft-conversion" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Planning Portal</a> for permitted development guidance.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Experience with St Neots old town and new estate properties</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Roof survey to confirm suitability before any commitment</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Staircase design that fits within your existing floor plan</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Build programming to minimise impact on daily life</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Popular Loft Conversion Types For St Neots Properties</h2>
          <p>We assess each roof individually and recommend what works best. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">loft conversion glossary</a> explains each option in plain terms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-types-grid">
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Dormer Conversion</h3>
            <p>Strong choice for St Neots terraces and semis wanting a proper bedroom with headroom. Creates the most usable floor area of any conversion type.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Velux Conversion</h3>
            <p>Uses roof windows without changing the roofline. Often works well for newer St Neots homes where permitted development limits external changes.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Hip To Gable</h3>
            <p>Best for end of terrace and semi detached homes wanting wider, more usable rooms by converting the hip section of the roof to a full gable wall.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-zone">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Areas We Cover Around St Neots</h2>
          <p>We serve St Neots and nearby Cambridgeshire communities, delivering consistent quality loft conversions across all property types.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-zone-grid">
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>St Neots Old Town</h3><p>Victorian terraces and Edwardian semis in the original town centre and riverside areas.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Eaton Socon and Eynesbury</h3><p>Established residential areas with a range of postwar and modern housing stock.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Wintringham and Loves Farm</h3><p>Newer development areas with modern detached and semi detached family homes.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Little Paxton and Great Paxton</h3><p>Village communities north of St Neots with traditional and modern properties.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-huntingdon/">Huntingdon</a></h3><p>Neighbouring market town with full coverage for all property types.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-st-ives-cambridgeshire/">St Ives</a></h3><p>Ouse Valley market town with period and modern housing across the area.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/">Cambridge</a></h3><p>Full Cambridge city and surrounding village coverage as part of our Cambridgeshire service.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Surrounding Villages</h3><p>We cover rural Cambridgeshire communities around St Neots including Tempsford and Abbotsley.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Why St Neots Homeowners Choose Truleum</h2>
          <p>Homeowners across St Neots and Cambridgeshire choose us for reliable delivery, honest quotes and quality results on every project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-proof-grid">
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-map-marked-alt"></i><h3>Local Team</h3><p>We understand St Neots housing, local planning context and site access requirements.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-file-signature"></i><h3>Transparent Quotes</h3><p>Detailed written quotes with no surprises. You know what is included before work starts.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i><h3>Fully Insured</h3><p>Full professional liability and site insurance throughout every project.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-award"></i><h3>Quality Finish</h3><p>Consistent attention to detail at every stage means a space you are genuinely proud of.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-faq">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>St Neots Loft Conversion FAQs</h2>
          <p>Common questions from St Neots homeowners. See our <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">2026 cost guide</a> for full Cambridgeshire pricing detail.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-faq-grid">
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How much does a loft conversion in St Neots cost?</h3>
            <p>Most projects in St Neots range from £28,000 to £64,000 depending on the conversion type, structural requirements and finishing specification chosen. We provide a written quote after a free site survey with no obligation.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Are new build homes in St Neots suitable for loft conversions?</h3>
            <p>It depends on the roof structure. Some newer homes have trussed rafters which are more complex to convert, while others have traditional cut timber roofs which are well suited. We check this during the survey stage before any commitment is made.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in St Neots?</h3>
            <p>Most conversions in St Neots are permitted development and do not require a planning application. Homes in any designated zones or requiring large roof alterations may need permission. We advise clearly on this from the outset.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How long does a St Neots loft conversion take?</h3>
            <p>A typical build runs from 6 to 10 weeks from start, depending on the type of conversion and level of finish required.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-cta">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);">Useful links: <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Loft Conversion Glossary</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cost Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Homeowner Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cambridge Area Page</a></p>
        <h2>Plan Your St Neots Loft Conversion Today</h2>
        <p>Book a free consultation to talk through your project, understand the options and get a clear cost picture. No pressure, no obligation.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Book Free Consultation <i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a loft conversion in St Neots cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most projects in St Neots range from £28,000 to £64,000 depending on conversion type, structural requirements and finishing specification."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are new build homes in St Neots suitable for loft conversions?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the roof structure. Some newer homes have trussed rafters which are more complex to convert. We assess this during the free survey."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in St Neots?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most conversions in St Neots are permitted development. Homes in designated zones or requiring major roof changes may need a planning application."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a St Neots loft conversion take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A typical build in St Neots runs from 6 to 10 weeks from start, depending on conversion type and finishing level."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
    </script>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
